course: dictionary
lesson: 3092
title: What is an effect?
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: An effect is what happens because of something else. The thing that makes it happen is the cause, and the effect is the result. «Antibiotics kill bacteria or stop them multiplying, and they have no effect on viruses.» The medicine is the cause, and what it does to bacteria, or doesn't do to viruses, is the effect.
explain: Films and shows have effects too. Effects are tricks of sound, light or pictures. A ghost effect can make a game character, called a sprite, look invisible. When we talk about cause and effect in science, we ask what happens and why.
explain: «In effect» is a useful phrase. It means really, or in practice. «Effect» can also be a formal verb: to effect a change means to make it happen. You will meet this in grown-up writing, so it is worth knowing.
fact: An effect is a change or result caused by something.
fact: Cause and effect: the cause makes the effect happen.
fact: «In effect» means really, or in practice.
fact: «Side effects» are unwanted effects, such as the unwanted effects of a medicine. Regulators watch for them after a medicine goes on sale.
fact: Effects in films and shows are tricks of sound, light or pictures, like special effects and sound effects.
exercise: What is an effect? | A tool for measuring heat | A word that means very old | *A change or result caused by something
exercise: «Regulators... side effects (unwanted effects) are watched for after it goes on sale». What are side effects? | Medicine given out by doctors | *Unwanted effects of a medicine | Happy surprises | Special tricks in a film
exercise: What does «in effect» mean? | Twice over | *Really, in practice | Without any sound | Inside a box
test: Which word means to make something happen, in a formal way? | To borrow | *To effect | To cover | To sleep
test: In «Antibiotics kill bacteria», what is the cause? | Bacteria | Doctors | *Antibiotics | Viruses
exam: Which sentence uses effect to mean a change or result? | *The rain had a big effect on the crops | Please effect the change before lunch | I will effect a cake for tea
